{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Aruch. Tsapeh hatsapit.</b> In my opinion it has no parallel, and its meaning is [known] by its melody." "And the meaning of <b>Arise, O princes</b> etc.: that Belshazzar was killed on that night, and Darius the Elder was anointed king. And the king is called מגן [shield] because he shields the people, likewise \"our shield, O Elohim\" (Psalms 84:10)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:27.966198196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}